# After I updated a new kernel (in auto update) and rebooted a machine, i got the Errror: 
    enclave_create with ENCLAVE_TYPE_SGX1 type failed (err=0x1) (oe_result_t=OE_PLATFORM_ERROR)
    
    1) This means that SGX kernel module needs to be reinstalled. Download and install the actual drivers from https://download.01.org/intel-sgx/linux-2.4/ubuntu18.04-server/

    2) then rebuild OE depdendent project - eEVM in build directory.

    3) rubuild the main project
    
    
# It is important to ensure that FLC-less machine does not have intel_sgx.ko driver installed. The only driver installed for such a machine should be isgx.ko. I accidentally installed both, then unpluged one from the kernel (by rmmod), but the problem is that it was not sufficient. The correct uninstallation of intel_sgx.ko is as follows:

    $ sudo systemctl stop aesmd.service
    $ sudo /sbin/modprobe -r intel_sgx
    ... delete all ocurrences of "intel_sgx.ko", especially the ones for the current kernel
    $ sudo /sbin/depmod
    $ sudo /bin/sed -i '/^intel_sgx$/d' /etc/modules

